If this is a brand-new repository

If you don't care about preserving the local commit history, the quickest fix is to start with a clean Git history after confirming .terraform is gone:

rm -rf .git

find . -type d -name ".terraform" -exec rm -rf {} +

cat > .gitignore <<EOF
.terraform/
**/.terraform/
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
EOF

git init
git checkout -b fix/module-workspace
git add .
git commit -m "Initial Terraform project"
git remote add origin git@github.com:sandeepsharma303/terraform.git
git push -u origin fix/module-workspace
